Why Lifecycle.PER_METHOD is preferred, because:

-it provides test isolation, so they can run in any order

-easy debugging when any test case fails

-safe for parallel execution

Go for Lifecycle.PER_CLASS only when:

-you want to shared state across test cases

-your test code is thread safe



